# Cross-Platform CMake Architecture & Toolchains

This skill enforces modern, target-based CMake standards (3.25+) and cross-compilation pipelines across Linux, Windows, macOS, and embedded targets.

---

## 📐 Core Architectures

1. **Target-Centric Modern CMake:** Pure target-based design (`target_include_directories`, `target_link_libraries`, `target_compile_definitions`) with zero global variable leaking.
2. **Cross-Compilation Toolchain Files:** Declarative `CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE` definitions for cross-compiling to Windows (via MinGW-w64 or Clang-CL) from Linux.
3. **Multi-Config Generators:** First-class support for `Ninja Multi-Config` and Visual Studio multi-configuration builds.
4. **Platform Abstraction Layer:** Clean separation between OS-specific implementations (`src/platform/linux/`, `src/platform/windows/`).
5. **Multiplatform Packaging via CPack:** Automated installer generation (NSIS/Wix for Windows, DEB/RPM/Tarball for Linux, DMG for macOS).

---

## 🛠️ 1. Modern Target-Centric `CMakeLists.txt`

```cmake
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.25)
project(CoreEngine VERSION 1.0.0 LANGUAGES CXX)

set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)
set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD_REQUIRED ON)
set(CMAKE_CXX_EXTENSIONS OFF)

# Platform detection
if(WIN32)
    set(PLATFORM_SOURCES src/platform/win32_system.cpp)
elseif(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
    set(PLATFORM_SOURCES src/platform/linux_system.cpp)
elseif(APPLE)
    set(PLATFORM_SOURCES src/platform/macos_system.mm)
endif()

add_library(core_engine STATIC
    src/engine.cpp
    ${PLATFORM_SOURCES}
)

target_include_directories(core_engine
    PUBLIC
        $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include>
        $<INSTALL_INTERFACE:include>
    PRIVATE
        src
)

# Compiler-specific warnings
target_compile_options(core_engine PRIVATE
    $<$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:MSVC>:/W4 /WX /permissive->
    $<$<NOT:$<CXX_COMPILER_ID:MSVC>>:-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Werror>
)
```

